    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "label": "supported",
      "paper_evidence": "We developed a note-grounded approach that uses large language model (LLM)-assisted reference construction, targeted and random human review, deterministic medication normalization, and semantic and temporal comparisons with structured medication history.",
      "reason": "Abstract, third sentence describes the framework components matching the claim."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "label": "supported",
      "paper_evidence": "These results show that note-to-structured-medication mismatch can arise from normalization errors, differences in terminology, and differences in documentation timing.",
